  "worked_solution": "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $R$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QR}=\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PM}+\\overset{\\to }{MT}+\\overset{\\to }{TR}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/c42a0b8323c282a573244591d900801194f2f5b7382aabe60dedd903b896a029.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QP}=b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PM}=-c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{MT}=d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{TR}=a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/9876c3c4947aa9d61e687138bfb6fb26040e7c334af8b02914f5857ae1616e98.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QR} & =\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PM}+\\overset{\\to }{MT}+\\overset{\\to }{TR} \\\\  & =b-c+d+a.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
